# ending contract specs passed
#   hall take placement flags ok
#   ⚠ ENDING AUDIO OUTSTANDING — all nine endings play the opening title theme.
#      ending.bed.sacrifice           bed        60-90s   The Seal. Containment: it closes over you, and the last thing to go is your own torch.
#      ending.bed.helped              bed        60-90s   He Tried to Help. The same closing, but somebody outside it was kind and it was not enough.
#      ending.bed.inversion           bed        60-90s   The Other Door. A building coming down, and a yard that is not there.
#      ending.bed.drugged             bed        60-90s   Cold, Bitter, Gone. Ordinary. A car park. Nothing wrong with the light, which is the frightening part.
#      ending.bed.surfaced            bed        60-90s   The Other Recordist. Two of them, on a service road, arriving in the morning.
#      ending.bed.contact-won         bed        45-70s   Open Channel. Source ends; the fatal return leaves forty-one seconds of breath on the recorder.
#      ending.bed.contact-lost        bed        30-55s   No Return. The carrier ends at the fault without a Horizon release.
#      ending.bed.tower-won           bed        60-90s   Exit Through the Gift Shop. Cathedral dust, severed bells, two bodies at an outward door.
#      ending.bed.tower-lost          bed        40-65s   The Full Peal. Eight bells complete the return through both bodies.
#      ending.strike.first            one-shot     4-8s   The 06:00 first strike. The demolition landing on the downbeat — the loudest thing in the game.
#      ending.room.silent             one-shot    6-12s   A room going properly silent: the moment the building stops having a signal in it.
#      ending.demolition.bed          bed        30-60s   Demolition, sustained: plant, hydraulics, masonry, at a distance and then not.
#      ending.demolition.collapse     one-shot    8-15s   One span letting go. For the inversion collapse, which is currently lens effects and prose.
